This module records which ticks a route was asked at, and splits them into on-peak and off-peak. It has
no tests: a hidden suite checks the behaviour below.

Keep these names and signatures:
- NewUsage(ticks ...int) *Usage
- (*Usage).OffPeak(from, to int) int
- (*Usage).Peak(from, to int) int
- InWindow(tick, from, to int) bool

Behaviour:
- Usage holds tick numbers.
- OffPeak(from, to) counts the ticks in the half-open window [from, to): a tick equal to from is inside,
  a tick equal to to is outside. A window with from >= to counts zero.
- Peak(from, to) counts every tick that is not in [from, to).

The behaviour is wrong in more than one file. Fix the code.
